cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite this software release for the LES-PME extensions and the
  upstream LES method paper listed in references for the underlying method.
type: software
title: "LES-PME: Trainable blocked and particle-mesh Ewald extensions to LES"
authors:
  - family-names: Cao
    given-names: Dehan
    email: caodehan@gmail.com
version: 0.2.0+lespme.1
date-released: 2026-11-03
repository-code: https://github.com/ListeningPost1379/les-pme
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
abstract: >-
  PyTorch extensions to Latent Ewald Summation with exact blocked
  recomputation, particle-mesh Ewald, multipoles and single induced
  responses, including force-loss double backward. Derived from
  ChengUCB/les at 35b971a650cf30adb84fef7138761e81aa47b3a2.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Latent Ewald summation for machine learning of long-range interactions"
    authors:
      - family-names: Cheng
        given-names: Bingqing
    journal: npj Computational Materials
    year: 2025
    volume: 11
    start: 80
    doi: 10.1038/s41524-025-01577-7
